# Bitwarden files that Multiwarden does not carry: Bitwarden's own developer tooling and
# repository automation (code owners, review and response bots). The upstream sync leaves
# changes to these paths out, so they stay removed. `*` also matches across folders, and
# `[x]` matches the letter x (used for the AI assistant configuration folder and files).
.[c]laude/*
*[C]LAUDE.md
.mcp.json
.github/CODEOWNERS
# Multiwarden's own community files replace Bitwarden's (issue and pull request templates,
# discussion categories).
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE
.github/DISCUSSION_TEMPLATE
.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
# Bitwarden's GitHub Actions workflows need Bitwarden's secrets and infrastructure, so none of
# them are carried, and new ones Bitwarden adds stay out. Multiwarden's own workflows
# (multiwarden-*.yml) are not in upstream, so they are unaffected.
.github/workflows/*
